#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:5
#: b1a3cff3c67a446d9bd138446e2a3511
msgid "QuadPlane Parameter setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:7
#: 67940916f9cf466daaa673c1525fc559
msgid "All QuadPlane specific parameters start with a \"Q\\_\" prefix. The parameters are very similar to the equivalent Copter parameters so if you are familiar with those you should find setting up a QuadPlane is easy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:13
#: ee07230ca1fe4ac6a4a9c9deed7ffdfd
msgid "Key Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:15
#: cef950276ef64f9bb65fdf00de94183d
msgid "To enable QuadPlane functionality you need to set the :ref:`Q_ENABLE<Q_ENABLE>` parameter to 1 and then refresh the parameter list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:17
#: a27ccde67dbd4dfa82af05266cc3817d
msgid "The :ref:`Q_M_PWM_MIN<Q_M_PWM_MIN>` and :ref:`Q_M_PWM_MAX<Q_M_PWM_MAX>` parameters used to set the PWM range of the VTOL motors (MOTORx) and the SERVOx_MIN/MAX for the outputs driving these motors is ignored. These need to be set to the range your ESCs expect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:20
#: 3fe0376a073741e3b32a33e4fec75ae0
msgid "The most critical tuning parameters are :ref:`Q_A_RAT_RLL_P<Q_A_RAT_RLL_P>` and :ref:`Q_A_RAT_PIT_P<Q_A_RAT_PIT_P>`. These default to 0.25 but you may find significantly higher values are needed for a QuadPlane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:23
#: 98b3ec9a63594ca1a41d5be66e96f1de
msgid "The :ref:`Q_M_SPIN_ARM<Q_M_SPIN_ARM>` parameter is important for getting the right level of motor output when armed in a quad mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:25
#: cbed586a52f9455b9e514b59b24739f5
msgid "It is recommended that you set :ref:`ARMING_RUDDER<ARMING_RUDDER>` to 2 to allow for rudder disarm. Alternatively you could have :ref:`MANUAL <manual-mode>` as one of your available flight modes (as that will shut down the quad motors). Please be careful not to use hard left rudder and zero throttle while flying or you risk disarming your motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:30
#: f0b3f261af7f424ab20f7de1798082cb
msgid "The default :ref:`SCHED_LOOP_RATE<SCHED_LOOP_RATE>` for a QuadPlane is to 300 (Hz). Most QuadPlanes do not need this to be raised. Some very small vehicles (< 1Kg) might benefit from setting it to 400. In heavier vehicles, their higher inertia results in lower effective control response rates, so they do not benefit from a higher loop rate. Raising above 300 only leads to larger log files in these vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:33
#: 5f390b72966b41ed9336bb8166e20955
msgid "Attitude Limiting Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:35
#: 3369db2141a44472910e234fca7c7ad7
msgid "The pitch and roll limits in VTOL modes are controlled by the lesser of :ref:`Q_A_ANGLE_MAX<Q_A_ANGLE_MAX>`, or the fixed wing limits (:ref:`PTCH_LIM_MAX_DEG<PTCH_LIM_MAX_DEG>`, :ref:`PTCH_LIM_MIN_DEG<PTCH_LIM_MIN_DEG>`, and :ref:` ROLL_LIMIT_DEG<ROLL_LIMIT_DEG>`), but conformance to only :ref:`Q_A_ANGLE_MAX<Q_A_ANGLE_MAX>` can be controlled with :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 14."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:37
#: 30deb3940d3d4a21a908ecd302e7bc6d
msgid "In addition, :ref:`Q_BCK_PIT_LIM<Q_BCK_PIT_LIM>` sets the maximum number of degrees of back or pitch up in Q modes when the airspeed is at :ref:`AIRSPEED_MIN<AIRSPEED_MIN>`, and is used to prevent excessive structural loads when pitching up to decelerate. The backwards/up pitch limit controlled by this parameter is in addition to limiting applied by the params above. The :ref:`Q_BCK_PIT_LIM<Q_BCK_PIT_LIM>` limit is only applied when :ref:`Q_FWD_THR_USE<Q_FWD_THR_USE>` is set to 1 or 2 and the vehicle is flying in a mode that uses forward throttle instead of forward tilt to generate forward speed. A value 0 to deactivates this limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:42
#: 8bb37abb7e074b719c52483abdb0e2e1
msgid "Return Behavior Setup Guide:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:44
#: de3d485a9d56482dbf6f8f1a3a0a76ed
msgid "While there are many parameters setting distances and heights for the various home return modes/behaviors (read about failsafes in :ref:`quadplane-flying` and :ref:`QRTL and RTL modes <quadplane-flight-modes>`), this is a quick setup guide for basic behaviors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:47
#: 6ea92bc08d834394a47cbda7c9f8f881
msgid "RTL mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:49
#: 10dd315f271945c58ee352043c566a64
msgid "Is a fixed wing return mode which normally flys back to the home point and loiters, but can optionally do an automatic mission sequence, usually set by the user to land the vehicle at home in fixed wing mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:51
#: 95cd9d78aaef45b0bfbe5cd9c955f1dc
msgid "If entered from VTOL flight several other behavior options can be selected by the :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:54
#: 7f63dc7dd54649cd8e9ba421a0c72495
msgid "QRTL mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:56
#: fb8f094a4f6f4e408cecf6aa63c0169b
msgid "When operating close to home is a VTOL return and the land at home, but further away will switch to fixed wing flight until back closer to home, and then transition back to VTOL and land at home. QRTL mode always results in a VTOL landing at home unless the pilot interrupts it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:59
#: 7055f116e71248bdbacafbb2765d17c0
msgid "RC Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:61
#: dfe10b82eb13422aa96ada995250d1d7
msgid "Loss of RC link can switch to a return flight mode or several other behaviors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:64
#: e88d03b86922435084e5748a0ff0f20e
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:66
#: 96d75e1bf77a4cb0b0885aad28f3a624
msgid "1.If you lose RC link for greater than :ref:`FS_LONG_TIMEOUT<FS_LONG_TIMEOUT>` in fixed wing flight set :ref:`FS_LONG_ACTN<FS_LONG_ACTN>` value below to obtain various behavior options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:68
#: 60b2bfb48abe47e0a75e246612a18e40
msgid "\"0\" : do nothing if in AUTO mode, otherwise switch to RTL mode (see #3,4 below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:69
#: ab16b70aad86433db3ed6dc33f4bbeb6
msgid "\"1\" : switch to RTL mode (see #3,4 below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:70
#: de79a6f768a64905983ffd5e3900ba08
msgid "\"2\" : cut throttle and glide in FWBA mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:71
#: aa2d62eff43e4e2881a5b238eda3f613
msgid "\"3\" : deploy parachute (assuming you have one setup)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:72
#: 5e4f7ef59068461da033e880af323995
msgid "\"4\" : switch to AUTO mode and execute mission at current mission sequence pointer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:74
#: 03afd08268c9465785240878b78c92f6
msgid "If you lose RC link for greater than :ref:`FS_LONG_TIMEOUT<FS_LONG_TIMEOUT>` in VTOL flight, you will immediately QLAND, unless you select the following optional behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:76
#: 84b3792b61a74971a4a1b37901fb6996
msgid "set :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 5 to switch to QRTL mode instead. (see #5 below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:77
#: 6539527a3f014b3e8ed7648fa9c1cf30
msgid "set :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 20 to switch to RTL mode instead (see #3,4 below). If bit 5 is set above, it will be ignored in lieu of this option bit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:79
#: d154056d436d4113bfdceb83778685bb
msgid "Anytime you switch to RTL (due either to manual mode change or failsafe action), do you want to execute an autoland sequence (does not need to actually have a land command, if some other action is desired), rather than just return and loiter around home?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:81
#: 97bdfcfd99b9415db91ae4d00525b308
msgid "If yes,then set up a DO_LAND_START mission sequence and enable the :ref:`RTL_AUTOLAND<RTL_AUTOLAND>` parameter. See :ref:`common-do-land-start` for details of setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:83
#: 2b3219886dec4075a8d824e98863dcfc
msgid "If in a VTOL mode, and you switch to RTL (due either to manual mode change or failsafe action), then set the :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` parameter value as follows to determine the behavior:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:85
#: e95b944e206748a68b6eb3313e59d83e
msgid "\"0\" : Switch to normal RTL mode, transitioning to fixed wing (see #3 above)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:86
#: 4e5a3b3d1a694a93a40042c214a01465
msgid "\"1\" : Transition to fixed wing, fly towards home, transition back to VTOL mode when close to home, move to over home, switch to QLAND and land at home in VTOL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:87
#: 272e8cb300e14b869b2fa428920015f3
msgid "\"2\" : Transition to fixed wing, fly towards home, loiter down to altitude around home, turn into the wind, transition back to VTOL mode and move to over home, switch to QLAND and land at home in VTOL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:88
#: 170778ea80fe4560842ec7c27b930c85
msgid "\"3\" : Switch to QRTL :Transition to fixed wing, and do a special approach to home including \"airbraking\",  transition back to VTOL mode, move to over home, switch to QLAND and land at home in VTOL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:90
#: 9cb88385cd3449bc86077b742bda62dd
msgid "When switching to QRTL  default behavior is to transition to fixed wing if in VTOL (assuming you are not close to home already in VTOL Flight), flying back to home, then switching back to VTOL as you approach home, switching to QLAND over home, and landing at home (see :ref:`qrtl-mode` for more information). You can disable the fixed wing approach, and return home and land only using VTOL mode if :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 16 set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:94
#: 986faff8c79d4ce9a741ca08a760d7ab
msgid "Q_OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:95
#: 26ecc622052742b9955b06342c0c7bd3
msgid "In addition, the behavior of QuadPlane can be modified by the setting of the :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bitmask parameter (no bits are set, by default):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:97
#: 860ca0274b744a519c1c37ab0e469d46
msgid "bit 0 (+1), if set, will force the transition from VTOL to Plane mode to keep the wings level and not begin climbing with the VTOL motors (as in a mission to a higher waypoint after VTOL takeoff) during the transition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:98
#: 5c927690ebad4dea930281152e6bab9d
msgid "bit 1 (+2), if set, will use a fixed wing takeoff instead of a VTOL takeoff for ground stations that can only send TAKEOFF instead of a separate VTOL_TAKEOFF mission command. Otherwise, QuadPlane will use VTOL takeoffs for a TAKEOFF mission command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:99
#: 6518ade1d33a48c8a116c84d6d7f288a
msgid "bit 2 (+4), if set, will use a fixed wing landing instead of a VTOL landing for ground stations that can only send LAND instead of a separate VTOL_LAND mission command. Otherwise, QuadPlane will use VTOL_LAND for a LAND mission command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:100
#: 68b34f80a5ef4e20b5cb42a9247c6b38
msgid "bit 3 (+8), if set, will interpret the takeoff altitude of a mission VTOL_TAKEOFF as specified when setup in Mission Planner (ie Relative to Home/Absolute {ASL}/Terrain {AGL}). Otherwise, it is relative to the takeoff point's altitude (AGL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:101
#: 8b6db803a6fd42189b0d7079a3fe20e7
msgid "bit 4(+16), if set, for “Always use FW spiral approach”  then during a VTOL_LAND mission command,instead of transitioning to VTOL flight and doing a VTOL landing, it will remain in plane mode, and proceed to the landing position, climbing or descending to the altitude set in the VTOL_LAND waypoint. When it reaches within :ref:`Q_FW_LND_APR_RAD<Q_FW_LND_APR_RAD>` of the landing location, it will perform a LOITER_TO_ALT to finish the climb or descent to that altitude set in the waypoint, then, turning into the wind, transition to VTOL mode and proceed to the landing location and land. Otherwise, a standard VTOL_LAND will be executed. See :ref:`quadplane-auto-mode` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:102
#: 435c67a400964f1f9fc9037d39f2323d
msgid "bit 5(+32), if set,  it will replace QLAND with QRTL for failsafe actions when in VTOL modes. See the Radio and Throttle Failsafe section of :ref:`quadplane-flying` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:103
#: 85b94bbcf54443efb5c84a6d7f19d99d
msgid "bit 6(+64), if set, will enforce the ICE idle governor even in MANUAL mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:104
#: 2c780b37984043838f9fa82a3df2c67d
msgid "bit 7(+128), if set, will force QASSIST to be active at all times in VTOL modes. See :ref:`Assisted Fixed-Wing Flight<assisted_fixed_wing_flight>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:105
#: 69b8f106079a496c8cb18ddb87770c4b
msgid "bit 8(+256), if set, QASSIST will only affect VTOL motors. If not set, QAssist will also use flying surfaces to stabilize(:ref:`Assisted Fixed-Wing Flight<assisted_fixed_wing_flight>` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:106
#: 183fb5c2b6504085a1fc967e7764ce24
msgid "bit 9(+512), if set, will enable AirMode (:ref:`airmode`) if armed via an RC switch. See :ref:`Auxiliary Functions<common-auxiliary-functions>` option value 41. This function has been deprecated as of Version 4.2. See new arming switch options in :ref:`common-auxiliary-functions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:107
#: b4c17e9e72df4d8081095e88eff92551
msgid "bit 10(+1024), if set, will allow the tilt servos to move with rudder input in vectored tilt setups while disarmed to determine range of motion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:108
#: 7a17ac3645d34d39abbe7185a5670542
msgid "bit 11(+2048), if set, will delay VTOL motor spin up until 2 seconds after arming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:109
#: 15b0a1b661e44740a3fbd005600294e4
msgid "bit 12(+4096), if set, disable speed based Qassist when using synthetic airspeed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:110
#: 093c17e8e68a4bce8e498c90b5da6e17
msgid "bit 13(+8192), if set, will disable Ground Effect Compensation of baro due to ground effect pressures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:111
#: aef17d30742947fa918f688675003191
msgid "bit 14(+16384), if set, ignore forward flight angle limits in Qmodes, otherwise :ref:`PTCH_LIM_MAX_DEG<PTCH_LIM_MAX_DEG>`, :ref:`PTCH_LIM_MIN_DEG<PTCH_LIM_MIN_DEG>`, and :ref:`ROLL_LIMIT_DEG<ROLL_LIMIT_DEG>` can constrain :ref:`Q_A_ANGLE_MAX<Q_A_ANGLE_MAX>` in VTOL modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:112
#: 807b85d9840b475cbc9f189e7c827393
msgid "bit 15(+32768), if set, will allow pilot to control descent during VTOL AUTO-LAND phases, similar to throttle stick action during QHOVER or QLOITER. However, this will not become active until the throttle stick is raised above 70% during the descent at least once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:113
#: c0e63f52feea40598674b06c3f050a24
msgid "bit 16(+65536), if set, will disable the fixed wing approach in QRTL mode and VTOL_LANDING mission items, see Hybrid RTL modes section of :ref:`quadplane-flying` for details of this hybrid landing approach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:114
#: 794d301294a841ae9e794d95e87bbade
msgid "bit 17(+131072), if set, will enable pilot horizontal re-positioning during VTOL auto LAND phases, momentarily pausing the descent while doing so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:115
#: b3d10521de7047bd8b172ad3d64b62a6
msgid "bit 18(+262144), if set, will only allow arming in VTOL and AUTO modes. This can be used for tailsitters to prevent arming in a fixed wing mode when sitting in VTOL stance to prevent tip-overs. For AUTO mode, WP must be a VTOL takeoff in order to arm with this option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:116
#: 4472e92c1f664474938a7fe7ed93db25
msgid "bit 19(+524288), if set, will allow the forcing of VTOL to Fixed Wing transitions if :ref:`Q_TRANS_FAIL<Q_TRANS_FAIL>` is not zero and exceeded, and if the airspeed is greater than 1/2 of :ref:`AIRSPEED_MIN<AIRSPEED_MIN>`, then the transition to fixed wing will immediately complete, rather than taking the :ref:`Q_TRANS_FAIL_ACT<Q_TRANS_FAIL_ACT>` action. See :ref:`quadplane-transitions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:117
#: c14b09fb16374dc6b32c99d418ccb569
msgid "bit 20(+1048576), if set overrides bit 5, if set, and forces an RTL on RC failsafe while in a VTOL mode. This is useful in over-water operations where either an QLAND or QRTL is undesirable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:118
#: a033a143be1047539cb343d646bc7e45
msgid "bit 21(+2097152), if set tilts tilt motors up when disarmed in FW modes (except manual) to prevent ground strikes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:119
#: 8199e05720b04d4192ce20ea6346aec2
msgid "bit 22(+4194304), if set scale fixed wing FF pid gains by the ratio of VTOL/fixed wing angle P gains in VTOL modes rather than reducing VTOL angle P based on airspeed. Used only if experiencing oscillations in back transitions at high airspeeds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:121
#: dd236b48a83346d3889b0e9e61448f77
msgid "Behavior can be modified as well as by the :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` and :ref:`Q_GUIDED_MODE<Q_GUIDED_MODE>` parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:123
#: fccc06f23a93495c9522e038532d7677
msgid "If you set :ref:`INITIAL_MODE<INITIAL_MODE>` to a VTOL mode, then switch to a fixed wing (other than MANUAL/ACRO/TRAINING) before arming, you will effectively be in a VTOL transition and when armed, the motors will spin up, and move, if tilted, to vertical."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-parameters.rst:127
#: 63162bf1608b457cbb01cf2bd563e497
msgid "The QuadPlane code requires GPS lock for proper operation. This is inherited from the plane code, which disables inertial estimation of attitude and position if GPS lock is not available. Do not try to fly a QuadPlane indoors. It will not fly well!!!!"
msgstr ""
